{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Elohim, You have rejected us</b> — the sense of זנחתנו is that we have not prevailed until now in battle, and likewise פרצתנו. And I have already mentioned that the force of the divine Name used in past and future is because events in battle befall [us], and likewise אנפת — the root אנף recurs for us."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {0 "The last phrase is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. 'Recur' attempts the obscure שובב, which may be corrupt. The clause כי תקרנה קורות במלחמה is also awkward and translated literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:20.804274144Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}